  "live_records": {
    "q-224988": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224988",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(7).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing values in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =7.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{0}{e}^{-7}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0009\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{0!}+\\frac{{7}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1}+\\frac{7\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0073\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
