    "q-224984": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224984",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(6).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing values in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =6.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{0}{e}^{-6}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0025\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{0!}+\\frac{{6}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1}+\\frac{6\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0174\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
