      "kp_id": "e-15057"
    },
    "q-224989": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224989",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(12).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing value in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0203\\,$ | $\\,0.0458\\,$ | $\\,0.0895\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $\\,0.2424\\,$ | $\\,0.3472\\,$ | $\\,0.4616\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =12.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X\\le 8) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =F(7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =0.0895+\\frac{{12}^{8}\\cdot {e}^{-12}}{8!} \\\\  & ≈0.1550\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
