    "q-224476": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224476",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(7).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing value in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $\\,0.9015\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =7.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(9) & =P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 8)+P(X=9) \\\\  & =F(8)+P(X=9) \\\\  & =0.7291+\\frac{{7}^{9}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{9!} \\\\  & ≈0.8305.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
