    "q-224998": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224998",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(12)$ given below, compute $P(X<11).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0895\\,$ | $\\,0.1550\\,$ | $\\,0.2424\\,$ | $\\,0.3472\\,$ | $\\,0.4616\\,$ | $\\,0.5760\\,$ | $\\,0.6815\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<11)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<11) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,10\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 10) \\\\  & =F(10) \\\\  & =0.3472.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
