    "q-224479": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224479",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1247\\,$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ | $\\,0.8666\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\le 6)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 6) & =F(6) \\\\  & =0.7622.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
