    "q-225056": {
      "dom_id": "step-q225056",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(3)$ given below, compute $P(1\\le X\\le 4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0498\\,$ | $\\,0.1991\\,$ | $\\,0.4232\\,$ | $\\,0.6472\\,$ | $\\,0.8153\\,$ | $\\,0.9161\\,$ | $\\,0.9665\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X\\le 4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 4) & =F(4)-F(0) \\\\  & =0.8153-0.0498 \\\\  & =0.7655.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
