    "q-225064": {
      "dom_id": "step-q225064",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5.5)$ given below, compute $P(1<X<7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0266\\,$ | $\\,0.0884\\,$ | $\\,0.2017\\,$ | $\\,0.3575\\,$ | $\\,0.5289\\,$ | $\\,0.6860\\,$ | $\\,0.8095\\,$ |\n\n$P(1<X<7)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X<7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1\\})+P(X\\in \\{2,3,4,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(1<X<7) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(1<X<7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<7) & =F(6)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.6860-0.0266 \\\\  & =0.6594.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
