    "q-224491": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224491",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(2)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.6767\\,$ | $\\,0.8571\\,$ | $\\,0.9473\\,$ | $\\,0.9834\\,$ | $\\,0.9955\\,$ | $\\,0.9989\\,$ | $\\,0.9998\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 4)=P(X>3).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =P(X>3) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-0.8571 \\\\  & =0.1429.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
