    "q-225083": {
      "dom_id": "step-q225083",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(7)$ given below, compute $P(X>9).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.8305\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ | $\\,0.9467\\,$ |\n\n$P(X>9)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>9) & =1-P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =1-F(9) \\\\  & =1-0.8305 \\\\  & =0.1695.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
